# Responsive Design Rules

## Non-negotiables

- Design the 320px layout first, then enhance at larger widths. Never treat `sm:` as "mobile".
- No horizontal overflow on `body` or any non-scroller container at any tested width.
- Minimum interactive target: 44x44 CSS px. Preferred control height: 48px (SOP is stricter than HIG).
- Minimum body text: 16px. Never use light/thin weights below 18px.
- Use `rem`, `clamp()`, `dvh`, and safe-area insets; avoid fixed pixel heights for text containers.
- Keep all essential content available at 200% zoom and 320px reflow.
- Intentional horizontal scrolling is allowed only inside the projects rail, with visible controls and an accessible fallback.

## Breakpoints

Use Tailwind defaults unless a proven need exists:

| Token | Min width | Primary use |
|---|---:|---|
| base | 0 | phone, single column |
| `sm` | 40rem / 640px | large phone, 2-up chips |
| `md` | 48rem / 768px | tablet, 2-column sections |
| `lg` | 64rem / 1024px | laptop, editorial split |
| `xl` | 80rem / 1280px | wide desktop |
| `2xl` | 96rem / 1536px | max-width polish only |

Test at 320, 375, 390, 768, 1024, 1280, 1440, and 1920px wide; plus 844x390 landscape.

## Layout patterns

- Page shell: `mx-auto w-full max-w-[80rem] px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-12`.
- Use CSS Grid/Flexbox, not absolute positioning, for primary layout.
- Use container queries for project cards so cards adapt to the rail, not only the viewport.
- Use `min-h-dvh` rather than `h-screen`; respect `env(safe-area-inset-*)` for floating mobile UI.
- Give sticky-header anchors `scroll-margin-top`.
- Long emails, URLs, and stack names must wrap: `overflow-wrap: anywhere`.
- Prefer `aspect-ratio` and intrinsic sizing over hard-coded media dimensions.

## Navigation and carousel

- Mobile nav must be a 48px trigger plus an accessible modal sheet/dialog; trap focus, close on Escape, restore focus, lock background scroll.
- Desktop nav must remain keyboard reachable and show a visible focus ring.
- Carousel: native horizontal scroll with `scroll-snap-type: x mandatory`, `overscroll-behavior-x: contain`, and `touch-action: pan-x`.
- Show one card plus a peek on phones, two plus peek on tablets, and 2.5-3 on desktop.
- Do not hide offscreen slides with `display: none`; keyboard focus must be able to reach every project.
- Provide Prev/Next buttons, index status, and arrow/Home/End key support.

## Anti-patterns

- `h-screen` on mobile browsers with dynamic chrome.
- Fixed heights around headings or cards containing text.
- `overflow-x: hidden` used to mask a layout bug.
- Tiny icon-only controls without a 44px hit area.
- Hover-only affordances or swipe-only interactions.
- Full-page scroll hijacking or snap on the document body.

## Verification

- Playwright viewport matrix for overflow, clipping, focus order, and touch targets.
- Check `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth` on every route.
- Keyboard-only pass at mobile and desktop widths.
- 200% browser zoom and 320px reflow pass.

